ext"},{"type":"text","value":">"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"returns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"any"}]}],"headings":[{"id":"type-parameters","text":"Type Parameters","level":2},{"id":"tcontext","text":"TContext","level":3},{"id":"parameters","text":"Parameters","level":2},{"id":"refs","text":"refs","level":3},{"id":"returns","text":"Returns","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\ntype JoinOnCallback<TContext> = (refs) => any;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/db/src/query/builder/types.ts:641](https://github.com/TanStack/db/blob/main/packages/db/src/query/builder/types.ts#L641)\n\nJoinOnCallback - Type for join condition callback functions\n\nThese callbacks receive refs for all available tables (including the newly\njoined table) and should return a boolean expression defining the join condition.\n\nImportant: The newly joined table is NOT marked as optional in this callback,\neven for left/right/full joins, because optionality is applied AFTER the join\ncondition is evaluated.\n\nExample: `(refs) => eq(refs.users.id, refs.orders.userId)`\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TContext\n\n`TContext` *extends* [`Context`](../interfaces/Context.md)\n\n## Parameters\n\n### refs\n\n[`RefsForContext`](RefsForContext.md)\\<`TContext`\\>\n\n## Returns\n\n`any`\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: JoinOnCallback\ntitle: JoinOnCallback\n---\n\n```ts\ntype JoinOnCallback<TContext> = (refs) => any;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/db/src/query/builder/types.ts:641](https://github.com/TanStack/db/blob/main/packages/db/src/query/builder/types.ts#L641)\n\nJoinOnCallback - Type for join condition callback functions\n\nThese callbacks receive refs for all available tables (including the newly\njoined table) and should return a boolean expression defining the join condition.\n\nImportant: The newly joined table is NOT marked as optional in this callback,\neven for left/right/full joins, because optionality is applied AFTER the join\ncondition is evaluated.\n\nExample: `(refs) => eq(refs.users.id, refs.orders.userId)`\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TContext\n\n`TContext` *extends* [`Context`](../interfaces/Context.md)\n\n## Parameters\n\n### refs\n\n[`RefsForContext`](RefsForContext.md)\\<`TContext`\\>\n\n## Returns\n\n`any`\n"}
